From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 21:27:46 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] mshtml: the legacy event object keeps what it is given

The event object's members that were E_NOTIMPL now work as in the
documentation: keyCode, button, reason, x, y, clientX/Y, offsetX/Y, screenX/Y,
alt/ctrl/shift keys, repeat, shiftLeft/altLeft/ctrlLeft, type, qualifier,
srcUrn, dataFld, propertyName, data, issession, srcElement, fromElement,
toElement, srcFilter, recordset, bookmarks and boundElements can be written
and read back, through every interface of the object. setAttribute,
getAttribute and removeAttribute keep named values (case-insensitive unless
the flag asks otherwise). contentOverflow, the IME members, behaviorCookie/
Part, wheelDelta, actionURL, buttonID, nextPage and dataTransfer answer with
the empty values of an event that is not of that kind instead of E_NOTIMPL;
keyboardLayout reports the layout of a keyboard event. get_cancelBubble no
longer dereferences the missing DOM event of a standalone event object.
returnValue reads true in IE9+ modes until a handler sets it. The mouse and
keyboard getModifierState, the mouse x/y and the keyboard locale answer.

diff --git a/dlls/mshtml/htmlevent.c b/dlls/mshtml/htmlevent.c
index 4eb1ae4..43968d3 100644
--- a/dlls/mshtml/htmlevent.c
+++ b/dlls/mshtml/htmlevent.c
